# Opaque dialogs

Confirmation dialogs, lightboxes, and other overlays must not look washed-out or let page content bleed through the panel.

## Required styling

- **Backdrop**: `bg-black/80` (not lighter opacities like `/55` or `/50`)
- **Dialog panel**: solid opaque background — prefer `bg-[#1a1410]` (matches existing sheet/image modals). Do not rely on semi-transparent panels.
- Prefer `shadow-2xl` for separation from the page behind

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="fixed inset-0 z-[230] flex items-center justify-center bg-black/80 p-4">
  <div className="w-full max-w-sm rounded-xl border border-surface-border bg-[#1a1410] p-4 shadow-2xl">
    …
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ BAD — panel/backdrop too transparent; list content shows through
<div className="fixed inset-0 … bg-black/55 p-4">
  <div className="… bg-surface-card/80 …">
```

Reference implementations: `ImagePreviewModal`, `UrlImagePreviewModal`, `CharacterStatModal`, and the delete confirm in `MyImagesList`.
